### Works with IntelliJ HTTP Client or VS Code "REST Client" extension.
### 1) Login as admin and copy the token into @token below

POST http://localhost:8081/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "username": "admin", "password": "admin123" }

###
@token = PASTE_TOKEN_HERE

### Register a normal user
POST http://localhost:8081/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{ "username": "ravi", "password": "secret123" }

### Who am I?
GET http://localhost:8081/api/users/me
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### List users (ADMIN only)
GET http://localhost:8081/api/users
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### List books (cached in Redis after first call)
GET http://localhost:8082/api/books
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Books grouped by author (Streams demo)
GET http://localhost:8082/api/books/by-author
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Add a book (ADMIN only)
POST http://localhost:8082/api/books
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "title": "Kafka: The Definitive Guide", "author": "Gwen Shapira", "price": 700, "stock": 4 }

### Place an order (replace BOOK_ID with an id from the book list)
POST http://localhost:8083/api/orders
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "bookId": "BOOK_ID", "quantity": 1 }

### My orders
GET http://localhost:8083/api/orders/my
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### My summary (Java 21 getFirst demo)
GET http://localhost:8083/api/orders/my/summary
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### All orders (ADMIN only)
GET http://localhost:8083/api/orders
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Circuit breaker state
GET http://localhost:8083/actuator/circuitbreakers

### Prometheus metrics
GET http://localhost:8083/actuator/prometheus
